To determine the average speed of the train over the entire trip, we use the formula for average speed:

$$
\text{Average Speed} = \frac{\text{Total Distance}}{\text{Total Time}}
$$

---

### Step 1: Calculate the Total Distance

The train travels:
- 150 km in the first part of the trip
- 90 km in the second part of the trip

$$
\text{Total Distance} = 150 \, \text{km} + 90 \, \text{km} = 240 \, \text{km}
$$

---

### Step 2: Calculate the Total Time

The train takes:
- 2.5 hours for the first part
- 1.5 hours for the second part

$$
\text{Total Time} = 2.5 \, \text{hours} + 1.5 \, \text{hours} = 4 \, \text{hours}
$$

---

### Step 3: Compute the Average Speed

$$
\text{Average Speed} = \frac{240 \, \text{km}}{4 \, \text{hours}} = 60 \, \text{km/h}
$$

---

### Final Answer

$$
\boxed{60}
$$
